# The DNS parity table: origin/main's DNS path against the DNS control and screen
# (refactor plan §2, slice 2's unit (b2), next/s2-parity; docs/engine/parity-dns.md).
# Generated by TestParity (pkg/screens/dns); make golden-update rewrites it. Do not edit.
# origin/main: pkg/characterization's goldens, read in place. The new path: hardn -g's plan
# and apply through the engine (the screen's Configure DNS leaves the same) and the screen's
# items, on hostfake with the screen tests' resolver model: written, not run (gate 5).
# Probes (commands that only read) are recorded, not compared.
# Sources: V<n> side-effects.md §8; decision <n> gallery-dns.md §4 (adopted 2026-10-22);
# P-37 (a) proposals.md; plan §3.19 (as amended 2026-10-22); side-effects row <n> (§3);
# control-dns.md, screen-dns.md and dns.md (docs/safety) by section.

== resolved on Debian 13
host: /etc/resolv.conf linked to resolved's stub, systemd-resolved running (forced: a stock Debian 13 keeps a regular file; Debian 12's cloud image links resolved's file)
origin/main: ops/dns_systemd_resolved/debian.golden (V1, V18, V19)
  probes: systemctl is-active systemd-resolved -> ok; which resolvconf -> error: fixture: resolvconf not installed
  write /etc/systemd/resolved.conf 0644, in place
    | [Resolve]
    | DNS=192.0.2.53 192.0.2.54
    | Domains=lan
  run systemctl restart systemd-resolved
  hardn -n: refused, exit status 2: hardn: -n/--dry-run only previews changes, so it can't be combined with -g/--configure-dns, which applies them. Nothing was changed.
new path: hardn -g's plan and apply; the screen's Configure DNS leaves the same
  probes: systemctl is-active systemd-resolved.service; resolvectl --no-pager dns; resolvectl --no-pager domain
  write /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d/zz-hardn.conf 0644, atomic
    | # Written by hardn: the system DNS servers for systemd-resolved.
    | # An empty assignment resets the list that earlier files built.
    | [Resolve]
    | DNS=
    | DNS=192.0.2.53 192.0.2.54
  mkdir /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d 0755
  chmod /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d 0755
  run systemctl try-reload-or-restart systemd-resolved.service
  backup: /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d/zz-hardn.conf (absent before: the rollback removes it); journal: journalled first; findings: DNS_PER_LINK
agree  refusal: none
agree  nameservers: 192.0.2.53, 192.0.2.54
agree  hardn.yml: not saved
differ files: /etc/systemd/resolved.conf 0644 | /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d/zz-hardn.conf 0644
       V19: resolved.conf overwritten whole; now a drop-in of hardn's own, resolved.conf untouched
differ search: Domains=lan | none set
       V19; decision 2: Domains=lan forced; now none set, the host's search domains kept
differ other lines: [Resolve] | # Written by hardn: the system DNS servers for systemd-resolved., # An empty assignment resets the list that earlier files built., [Resolve]
       V19; dns.md §2.7: resolved.conf's section; now the drop-in's, under two lines saying it is hardn's
differ directories: none | /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d 0755, chmod /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d 0755
       V19; dns.md §2.12: the drop-in's directory, set 0755 whatever the umask
differ commands: systemctl restart systemd-resolved | systemctl try-reload-or-restart systemd-resolved.service
       V19; dns.md §2.7, §3: a restart; now a reload on systemd 256 and later, a restart before (Ubuntu 24.04)
differ write: in place | atomic
       V18: written in place; now replaced whole by a rename
differ backup: none | /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d/zz-hardn.conf (absent before: the rollback removes it)
       V18: nothing recorded; now the drop-in is recorded absent, so a rollback removes it
differ journal: none | journalled first
       V18: no rollback; now journalled first, so a failure rolls it back
differ findings: none | DNS_PER_LINK
       P-37 (a); control-dns.md §2.6, §8 D1; decision 5: eth0's own DHCP server, which resolved still queries, reported
differ dry run: the service writes and runs as live (cfg.DryRun unread below the menus); no path reaches it: hardn -n refused (exit status 2) | the plan alone: nothing written
       V1: no path reaches the service's dry run (the menu's Configure only prints); a dry run is now the plan alone
v0.3.2: the same file and restart, backed up first (V18, V19: regressed); -n -g ran the probes only (V1: regressed; P0.8 refuses -n -g now); menu 3 asked y/n first (regressed: gallery-dns.md §7)

