== resolved on Alpine 3.23
host: /etc/resolv.conf linked to resolved's stub, systemd-resolved running (cannot exist: Alpine has no systemd)
origin/main: ops/dns_systemd_resolved/alpine.golden (V1, V18, V19)
  probes: systemctl is-active systemd-resolved -> ok; which resolvconf -> error: fixture: resolvconf not installed
  write /etc/systemd/resolved.conf 0644, in place
    | [Resolve]
    | DNS=192.0.2.53 192.0.2.54
    | Domains=lan
  run systemctl restart systemd-resolved
  hardn -n: refused, exit status 2: hardn: -n/--dry-run only previews changes, so it can't be combined with -g/--configure-dns, which applies them. Nothing was changed.
not compared: systemd-resolved cannot run on Alpine 3.23, whose init is openrc (dns.HostOf: Systemd no; docs/safety/dns.md §2.1); there origin/main takes the direct strategy (direct on Alpine 3.23)

